1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:20,000
DRIFTLINE — Change-to-action operations
Live Cloud Run demo · synthetic fixture clearly labelled

2
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:50,000
One verified source change maps to four downstream artifacts.
High-risk work pauses for a named human decision.

3
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Evidence is visible before action: removed language, added language,
the synthetic source ID, and a SHA-256 snapshot hash.

4
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The impact map keeps owners, bounded actions, and risk visible.
The model proposes; deterministic policy owns the approval boundary.

5
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Approve resumes the workflow: two published, one owner review, one scheduled.
The named operator and durable audit event are recorded.

6
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Activity shows every stage, outcome, timestamp, and audit event ID.
The workflow is resumable rather than another alert or chat window.

7
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Undo returns the workflow to the approval gate and restores draft states.
The ADK agent has no approval or publish tool.

8
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:50,000
LIVE GOOGLE PATH VERIFIED · Gemini 3.5 Flash + Google ADK · Cloud Run + Firestore
Allowlisted inspect/state tools · deterministic human gate
